{
  "_comment": "Race roster, transcribed from RACES.md (which stays the human-readable source of truth for the design rationale). All stats and labor skills run 1-10 on the Human Peasant = 5 scale; walk_speed and food_per_meal are racial constants with no per-recruit variance (FOUNDATION_SPEC section 3). 'category' is what the race offers (Warrior/Economy/Research/Foraging/Versatile/Labor) and drives the first-run category-spread guarantee plus which stat gets the 5% exceptional roll. 'alignment' is data, not a moral system -- it drives recruit-event weighting and later good/evil friction. 'rarity' is the base recruit-offer weight (Common 60 / Uncommon 30 / Rare 10, shifting toward Uncommon/Rare as settlement Power grows); 'player-made' and 'not recruitable' never appear in recruit offers. 'housing_style' is the fund-a-house placement rule the recruit picks their own spot by. 'rivalries' lists specific race ids with a starting-relationship penalty; on top of these there is a mild blanket penalty between any Good-aligned and any Evil-aligned pair, which is derived from 'alignment' rather than listed per race. Non-'_' keys are races; human_peasant is the 1-10 measuring stick and is deliberately not recruitable.",
  "_comment_sprites": "'sprite' is the on-map token art, commissioned, in 'Official Sprites/' at 1254px square (Skeleton_Worker is 1024). The mapping lives here rather than in a Dictionary in Main.gd so adding a race is a data edit. Tokens scale it down to ~32-40px on screen; see FollowerToken/WorkerToken. human_peasant has no sprite on purpose -- it is the not-recruitable measuring stick and never gets a token. THREE VARIANTS EXIST BUT ARE DELIBERATELY NOT WIRED: Orc_Armed.png, Goblin_Armed.png and Gray_Dwarf_Miner.png. They are for future per-state art -- armed versions for when combat exists (Stage 4+), the miner for a working/at-node state -- and there is no state machine to select them yet. Wiring them now would mean inventing a state concept purely to justify the art.",
  "_derivation": {
    "divisor": 2,
    "formula": "effective_skill = clamp(skill + floor((governing_attribute - 5) / divisor), min, max)",
    "max": 10,
    "min": 1
  },
  "_generated_by": "tools/export_roster.gd from docs/design/stat_rework_roster.xlsx -- do not hand-edit the stat blocks",
